<title>USA: Turkish Airlines announces new route.</title>
<headline>Turkish Airlines announces new route.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>National carrier Turkish Airlines will start flying a new direct route from Chicago to Istanbul beginning 7 May.</p>
<p>Reggie Bal, Cargo Sales Manager for U.S. Operations, based at John F.Kennedy airport in New York, said the carrier will fly three Airbus 340's on a Wednesday, Friday and Sunday schedule.</p>
<p>Cargo closeout times of each flight are to be given by Monday 3 March.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
